chat messages\n    60→   - Copy room link to invite others\n    61→\n    62→## 🏗️ Project Structure\n    63→\n    64→```\n    65→videocalling.app/\n    66→├── app/\n    67→│   ├── components/       # Vue components\n    68→│   │   ├── Header.vue\n    69→│   │   └── LanguageSwitcher.vue\n    70→│   ├── composables/      # Composable functions\n    71→│   │   └── useWebRTC.js\n    72→│   ├── pages/            # Application pages\n    73→│   │   ├── index.vue     # Homepage\n    74→│   │   └── room/\n    75→│   │       └── [id].vue  # Video room page\n    76→│   └── app.vue           # Root component\n    77→├── assets/\n    78→│   └── styles/           # SCSS styles\n    79→│       ├── main.scss\n    80→│       └── variables.scss\n    81→├── locales/              # i18n translations\n    82→│   ├── en.json\n    83→│   ├── zh.json\n    84→│   ├── ja.json\n    85→│   └── es.json\n    86→├── public/               # Static files\n    87→└── nuxt.config.ts        # Nuxt configuration\n    88→```\n    89→\n    90→## 🔧 Configuration\n    91→\n    92→### Adding a New Language\n    93→\n    94→1. Create a new locale file in `locales/` (e.g., `fr.json`)\n    95→2. Add the locale to `nuxt.config.ts`:\n    96→\n    97→```typescript\n    98→i18n: {\n    99→  locales: [\n   100→    // ... existing locales\n   101→    { code: 'fr', language: 'fr-FR', name: 'Français', file: 'fr.json' }\n   102→  ]\n   103→}\n   104→```\n   105→\n   106→## 🌐 WebRTC & PeerJS\n   107→\n   108→This application uses PeerJS for simplified WebRTC peer-to-peer connections. In the current implementation:\n   109→\n   110→- PeerJS public server is used for signaling\n   111→- Room management uses localStorage (for demo purposes)\n   112→- Peer-to-peer video/audio streaming\n   113→\n   114→### Production Considerations\n   115→\n   116→For production use, consider:\n   117→\n   118→1. **Signaling Server**: Implement a proper signaling server (Socket.io/WebSocket)\n   119→2. **TURN Servers**: Add TURN servers for better connectivity\n   120→3. **Room Management**: Use a backend for room state management\n   121→4. **Security**: Add authentication and authorization\n   122→5. **Scalability**: Implement Selective Forwarding Unit (SFU) for larger rooms\n   123→\n   124→## 🤝 Contributing\n   125→\n   126→Contributions are welcome! Feel free to:\n   127→\n   128→- Report bugs\n   129→- Suggest new features\n   130→- Submit pull requests\n   131→\n   132→## 📄 License\n   133→\n   134→MIT License - feel free to use this project for any purpose.\n   135→\n   136→## 🙏 Acknowledgments\n   137→\n   138→- Built with [Nuxt 3](https://nuxt.com/)\n   139→- WebRTC powered by [PeerJS](https://peerjs.com/)\n   140→- Icons from custom SVG designs\n   141→\n   142→---\n   143→\n   144→Made with ❤️ for the open-source community\n   145→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a7bf39e-4091-474e-b8f1-7183a43538fc","uuid":"2f581df4-b9b4-4c06-bc74-5bbf9b3c6b98","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/airyland/workspace/becool/videocalling.app/README.md","content":"# Video Calling App 📹\n\nA free, open-source video calling application built with Nuxt 3 and WebRTC. No registration required - just create a room and start calling!\n\n## ✨ Features\n\n- 🎥 **HD Video Calls** - Crystal clear video quality\n- 🔒 **Secure & Private** - Peer-to-peer connections using WebRTC\n- 🌍 **Multi-language** - Support for English, Chinese, Japanese, and Spanish\n- 💬 **Real-time Chat** - Send messages during calls\n- 🖥️ **Screen Sharing** - Share your screen with others\n- 📱 **Responsive Design** - Works on desktop and mobile\n- 🚀 **No Account Needed** - Start calling instantly\n\n## 🛠️ Tech Stack\n\n- **Frontend Framework**: Nuxt 3\n- **Internationalization**: @nuxtjs/i18n\n- **WebRTC**: PeerJS\n- **Styling**: SCSS with custom design system\n- **Real-time Communication**: WebRTC (peer-to-peer)\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install\n```\n\n### Development\n\nStart the development server on `http://localhost:3000`:\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n### Production Build\n\n```bash\nnpm run build\nnpm run preview\n```\n\n## 📖 How to Use\n\n1. **Create a Room**\n   - Click \"Create Room\" on the homepage\n   - You'll be redirected to a unique room with a shareable link\n\n2. **Join a Room**\n   - Enter the room code on the homepage and click \"Join Room\"\n   - Or open the shared room link directly\n\n3. **During the Call**\n   - Toggle your video/audio on/off\n   - Share your screen\n   - Send chat messages\n   - Copy room link to invite others\n\n## 🏗️ Project Structure\n\n```\nvideocalling.app/\n├── app/\n│   ├── components/       # Vue components\n│   │   ├── Header.vue\n│   │   └── LanguageSwitcher.vue\n│   ├── composables/      # Composable functions\n│   │   └── useWebRTC.js\n│   ├── pages/            # Application pages\n│   │   ├── index.vue     # Homepage\n│   │   └── room/\n│   │       └── [id].vue  # Video room page\n│   └── app.vue           # Root component\n├── assets/\n│   └── styles/           # SCSS styles\n│       ├── main.scss\n│       └── variables.scss\n├── locales/              # i18n translations\n│   ├── en.json\n│   ├── zh.json\n│   ├── ja.json\n│   └── es.json\n├── public/               # Static files\n└── nuxt.config.ts        # Nuxt configuration\n```\n\n## 🔧 Configuration\n\n### Adding a New Language\n\n1. Create a new locale file in `locales/` (e.g., `fr.json`)\n2. Add the locale to `nuxt.config.ts`:\n\n```typescript\ni18n: {\n  locales: [\n    // ... existing locales\n    { code: 'fr', language: 'fr-FR', name: 'Français', file: 'fr.json' }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## 🌐 WebRTC & PeerJS\n\nThis application uses PeerJS for simplified WebRTC peer-to-peer connections. In the current implementation:\n\n- PeerJS public server is used for signaling\n- Room management uses localStorage (for demo purposes)\n- Peer-to-peer video/audio streaming\n\n### Production Considerations\n\nFor production use, consider:\n\n1. **Signaling Server**: Implement a proper signaling server (Socket.io/WebSocket)\n2. **TURN Servers**: Add TURN servers for better connectivity\n3. **Room Management**: Use a backend for room state management\n4. **Security**: Add authentication and authorization\n5. **Scalability**: Implement Selective Forwarding Unit (SFU) for larger rooms\n\n## 🤝 Contributing\n\nContributions are welcome! Feel free to:\n\n- Report bugs\n- Suggest new features\n- Submit pull requests\n\n## 📄 License\n\nMIT License - feel free to use this project for any purpose.\n\n## 🙏 Acknowledgments\n\n- Built with [Nuxt 3](https://nuxt.com/)\n- WebRTC powered by [PeerJS](https://peerjs.com/)\n- Icons from custom SVG designs\n\n---\n\nMade with ❤️ for the open-source community\n","numLines":145,"startLine":1,"totalLines":145}}}
